                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "On the 36th anniversary of the Tiananmen Square Massacre, we remember the thousands of students and civilians who bravely took to the streets to peacefully protest and exercise their freedoms of expression in pursuit of democracy, human rights, and an end to corruption.\n\nAs the world witnessed, the CCP brutally cracked down on unarmed civilians in an attempt to suppress pro-democracy dissent.\n\nThirty-six years later, we must never forget their courage, and we must continue to speak out against the ongoing repression still inflicted against the Falun Gong, Uyghurs, Christians, pro-democracy activists, and many other persecuted groups in Communist China.",
